  "query_preview": "..(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 547 PM EDT MON JUL 20 2026\n\nThe models are in good agreement with an amplified and stagnant \nlong wave pattern to rule over the CONUS through early next week. \nThe center of a seasonably strong upper level ridge will meander \nfrom the southern Plains to the Four Corners region, while broader \ntroughing modulates east of the Mississippi River. This will result \nin a reprieve from the humidity across the Ohio and Tennessee \nvalleys through the middle of the week. Humidity will be on the \nincrease once again across the region by this weekend and into early \nnext week. \n\nOn Wednesday, a surface cold front will be exiting into Tennessee, \nwith enough low level moisture lingering to allow for some renewed \nconvection, especially across far southeastern Kentucky. High \npressure builds in more decisively Wednesday night, with welcomed \nnortheasterly low level winds ushering in much lower dew points than \nwe have seen lately. Some fog will likely occur following the \nmultiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms seen across the area, \nalthough the pressure gradient may limit this coverage. Drier and \ncooler weather will be in full swing on Thursday. \n\nAs troughing sharpens back up over the Ohio Valley, bouts of \nshort wave energy will be moving southeast within the established \nnorthwesterly flow aloft. Model details regarding timing are lower\nconfidence this far out, but rain chances will return as some \nmoderate moisture advection occurs in the low levels, with LREF \nmean PWATs of 1.4 to 1.5 inches nosing back into southeastern \nportions of the Commonwealth by Friday. PoPs look to peak Friday \nnight into Saturday, with somewhat better model agreement on \nincreased mid and upper level forcing in place. For the rest of \nthe weekend and early next week, despite the favorable stormier \ntrack that northwest flow can mean aloft, mean PWATS right now \nremain in the 50th to 75th percentile, so only slight to chance \nPoPs are in the forecast for Sunday through Monday. \n\nHighs will retreat to the upper 70s to lower 80s Wednesday and \nThursday, before gradually warming to the mid to upper 80s by \nMonday. Overnight lows will moderate from the upper 50s and low 60s \nmid-week, to the upper 60s and around 70 by early next week.",
